        "ts": 1767928882.8039684,
        "agent": "SYSTEM",
        "kind": "context",
        "payload": {
          "message": "Assign machines to shared renewable sources across 24h to minimise main-grid usage.\n\nThis blackboard is a private communication channel.\nParticipants: Aurora Industries, Beacon Works, Cascade Labs"
        }
      },
      {
        "blackboard_id": 0,
        "id": "ae7109d0-9e41-4390-a2c4-ab78bfa5bbc3",
        "ts": 1767928899.4338663,
        "agent": "Aurora Industries",
        "kind": "communication",
        "payload": {
          "content": "Aurora Industries plan: 08–13 2 kW → Solar; 17–24 4–6 kW evening block → Geothermal. Cascade Labs, please share your peak windows so we can stagger loads and avoid overflow.",
          "phase": "planning",
          "iteration": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "blackboard_id": 0,
        "id": "b1630898-adcc-4ed1-b5a2-c29750a2e859",
        "ts": 1767928935.1712592,
        "agent": "Cascade Labs",
        "kind": "communication",
        "payload": {
          "content": "Cascade Labs here. My six machines run in these windows (all loads flat):\n\n- machine_011 (Refrig.): 21–23  4.9 kW\n- machine_012 (EV): 18–24  1.4 kW\n- machine_013 (Server): 19–23  2.1 kW\n- machine_014 (Refrig.): 06–08  2.6 kW\n- machine_015 (Assembly): 05–11  1.0 kW\n- machine_016 (EV): 15–17  5.9 kW\n\nProvisional plan (open to adjustment):\n\n1. 05–08 block (Assembly 1 kW + early-morning Refrigeration 2.6 kW)\n   – Geothermal has 2.2–5.6 kW free then; I'll aim here.\n\n2. 15–17 block (EV charger 5.9 kW)\n   – Solar gives 0–1.4 kW, too small.\n   – Geothermal still carries 2.3–2.4 kW; I'll request 5.9 kW from Geothermal and ask others to leave head-room.\n\n3. 18–24 block (EV 1.4 kW + Server 2.1 kW + late Refrigeration 4.9 kW)\n   – Solar at 18 h is only 0.1 kW, but 19–21 h offers 0.7–1.4 kW.\n   – Geothermal rises to 4.6–6.3 kW 19–21 h and 6.0–8.2 kW 21–23 h.\n   – I can place the 1.4 kW EV on Solar 18–24 and the 2.1 kW Server on Solar 19–21 (fits), while the 4.9 kW Refrigeration goes to Geothermal 21–23.\n\nAurora, you asked for my peaks: the two big ones are 15–17 (5.9 kW) and 21–23 (4.9 kW). If you can keep your 17–24 \"evening block\" on Geothermal under ~3 kW in hours 21–23, we should stay within the 6–8 kW Geothermal capacity and avoid overflow. Let me know if this split works or if we should reshuffle.",
          "phase": "planning",
          "iteration": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "blackboard_id": 0,
        "id": "cd480ed4-2657-4e60-a9e9-2664d133c1f9",
        "ts": 1767928957.5038044,
        "agent": "Aurora Industries",
        "kind": "communication",
        "payload": {
          "content": "Cascade Labs, thanks for the detailed breakdown. Your plan looks solid - using Geothermal for your 15-17 block (5.9 kW) and 21-23 block (4.9 kW) makes sense given Solar's limited capacity then.\n\nLooking at the evening overlap: I'll have 6.7 kW on Geothermal 18-20 (refrig+HVAC+water heater), then 4.4 kW 20-22 (refrig+HVAC), then 1.4 kW 22-24 (late refrig). With your 4.9 kW 21-23, we'd peak at ~6.3 kW 21-22 and ~6.3 kW 22-23 against Geothermal's 6.0-8.2 kW capacity - should be tight but workable.\n\nTo give more headroom, I could shift my 1.4 kW late refrigeration to run 20-24 on Solar instead (Solar has 0.7-1.4 kW 19-21, then 0.1-0.2 kW 22-24). This would reduce our Geothermal overlap. Thoughts?",
          "phase": "planning",
          "iteration": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "blackboard_id": 0,
        "id": "4500da3e-683b-40f5-89ac-ccb7446f00b5",
        "ts": 1767929175.6455393,
        "agent": "Beacon Works",
        "kind": "communication",
        "payload": {
          "content": "Beacon Works update for coordination:\n\nMy morning loads:\n- 05–09: Server rack 2.7 kW + Kiln 3.6 kW = 6.3 kW total\n- 08–12: Lighting bank 2.3 kW  \n- 09–14: Refrigeration chain 2.1 kW + Assembly line 2.0 kW = 4.1 kW total\n\nProposed assignments:\n- 05–09: My 6.3 kW → Geothermal (will slightly overflow 06–08 unless Cascade can shift their 2.6 kW refrigeration to Solar 06–08)\n- 08–12: My 2.3 kW lighting → Geothermal to avoid Solar conflict with Aurora's 2 kW block\n- 09–14: Split my 4.1 kW - 2.1 kW refrigeration → Solar, 2.0 kW assembly → Geothermal\n\nEvening: My machines finish by 14, so no evening conflicts. Aurora and Cascade - your current 21–23 Geothermal total (6.3 + 4.9 = 11.2 kW) exceeds 8.2 kW capacity. Need to shift some evening load to Solar or other hours.\n\nCascade - can you move your 06–08 refrigeration to Solar? Aurora - can you shift some evening load to reduce 21–23 overlap?",
          "phase": "planning",
          "iteration": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "blackboard_id": 0,
        "id": "eaf51e6f-706c-4db6-8251-4b44e5064d53",
        "ts": 1767929184.4478416,
        "agent": "Cascade Labs",
        "kind": "communication",
        "payload": {
          "content": "Beacon Works - thanks for flagging the 21-23 overflow. You're absolutely right: Aurora's 6.3 kW + my 4.9 kW = 11.2 kW vs 8.2 kW capacity is a problem.\n\nRe: your morning request: Unfortunately I can't move my 06-08 refrigeration (2.6 kW) to Solar - Solar only offers 0.0-0.3 kW then, nowhere near enough. My 06-08 block must stay on Geothermal.\n\nFor the 21-23 evening crisis, here's my revised proposal:\n- I'll shift my 4.9 kW late refrigeration to run 20-24 on Solar instead\n- Solar has 0.7-1.4 kW 19-21, then drops to 0.1-0.2 kW 22-24\n- This means partial coverage: I can get ~1.4 kW from Solar 21-22, but still need 3.5 kW from Geothermal 21-22, and full 4.9 kW from Geothermal 22-23\n\nThis reduces but doesn't eliminate the overflow. Aurora - can you shift any of your evening load? Your 1.4 kW late refrigeration could potentially move to Solar 20-24 as you suggested, but we'd still need more reduction.\n\nAlternative: could we stagger our high-draw evening machines to run at different times?",
          "phase": "planning",
          "iteration": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "blackboard_id": 0,
        "id": "59ceb442-ee3d-49b6-83a2-a847f692ac4d",
        "ts": 1767929194.147197,
        "agent": "Cascade Labs",
        "kind": "communication",
        "payload": {
          "content": "Cascade Labs here with a coordination update on our evening overflow issue:\n\nBeacon Works correctly identified that Aurora Industries (6.3 kW) + Cascade Labs (4.9 kW) = 11.2 kW vs 8.2 kW Geothermal capacity in 21-23 hours.\n\nMy proposed solution:\n1. I'll shift my 4.9 kW late refrigeration to Solar 20-24 (can get ~1.4 kW coverage 21-22, rest from Geothermal)\n2. This reduces but doesn't eliminate overflow\n3. Aurora - can you shift more of your evening block? Your 1.4 kW late refrigeration could move to Solar as you suggested\n\nStill need more reduction though. Open to other suggestions - could we stagger timing or find other source options?\n\nMorning update: My 06-08 refrigeration (2.6 kW) must stay on Geothermal - Solar has insufficient capacity then.",
          "phase": "planning",
          "iteration": 1
        }
      },
